-- Q7: Risk Assessment [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under AU-C 315, the risk of material misstatement (RMM) comprises inherent risk and control risk. Inherent risk is the susceptibility of an assertion to misstatement before considering controls, while control risk is the risk that controls will not prevent or detect a misstatement.
Wrong (A): Audit risk is the overall risk model (RMM multiplied by detection risk), not a component of RMM itself.
Wrong (C): Sampling risk and nonsampling risk relate to the auditor''s procedures, not the entity''s risk of misstatement.
Wrong (D): Business risk and information risk are general concepts not part of the audit risk model defined in AU-C 315.$EXPL$
