-- Q9: Risk Assessment [hard/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under AU-C 315.26, the auditor must identify and assess risks of material misstatement by understanding the entity''s environment, including changes in operations. Simultaneous changes in accounting policy and ERP systems create compound risks — new processes may contain errors, staff may lack training on revised policies, and data migration introduces misstatement possibilities.
Wrong (B): Treating simultaneous policy and system changes as routine ignores the compounding effect on risk recognized by AU-C 315.A30.
Wrong (C): Increased risk does not require withdrawal; AU-C 330 requires designing enhanced audit procedures in response.
Wrong (D): These changes elevate both inherent risk (incorrect policy application) and control risk (untested system controls), not control risk alone.$EXPL$
